CORE
main.c
--signed-overflow-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main.overflow.1\] line 4 arithmetic overflow on signed + in a + b: FAILURE$
^\[main.overflow.2\] line 5 arithmetic overflow on signed - in a - b: FAILURE$
^\[main.overflow.3\] line 6 arithmetic overflow on signed \* in a \* b: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Signed operations wider than 32 bits must get an overflow check: the check
used to be restricted to 32-bit signed operations.
